title The front door in Bhakta
prompt Keaton: rewrite the root readme in Bhakta and all recursive links down to leaves that are meant for Bhakta rather than Gauge, with a draft for guidance.
rota lap 4325, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears. The lap opened on a register nobody could find and closed with it on the front door.
think Keaton's draft is not a specification, it is a VOICE SAMPLE -- a forest and six senses, a bowling alley with bumper lanes, a copy-paste prompt that asks nothing personal, an age recommendation, and jewels turning into fabric. Read as Bhakta it is exact: a newcomer greeted, no background assumed, and the whole thing rooted to Atthowe ecology by its one prompt.
think So the rewrite carried his words rather than paraphrasing them, and the reference half of the page -- contents, what runs today, the generated metrics block, how the tree is organised -- stayed as it was, because that half is properly Gauge and a front door is allowed two registers if it says which is which.
obs THE GENERATED BLOCK SURVIVED, WHICH IS THE FIRST THING TO CHECK WHEN REWRITING A PAGE A TOOL ALSO WRITES. readme_metrics owns lines between its own markers; the rewrite went above them and the tool re-wrote its block afterward without complaint.
obs THE FRONT DOOR NOW GRADES 93 AND THE FIRST HOUR 95, BOTH AT THE DOOR SETTING. Register 86 and 87, which clears the strict ceiling of 80 that the Door setting keeps -- so both pages pass the register they now claim, which is the whole test a page naming Bhakta has to survive.
obs AND I STOPPED AT TWO PAGES ON PURPOSE, WHICH IS THE RULING RATHER THAN THE LIMIT. The README links five teaching children and four of them carry NO Style line at all. Stamping Bhakta on a page I have not rewritten is exactly the mistake the 47 Radiant pages would have been, ruled on an hour earlier in this same sitting. A register is earned by being written in, so the two pages I actually wrote carry it and the rest wait for a hand.
obs THE ONE I CHOSE IS THE ONE THE README CALLS JOIN HERE. Following his instruction to reach the leaves meant for Bhakta rather than every leaf, and the first hour is the direct next step from the front door -- onboarding, which Bhakta's own room list names first.
obs ITS OPENING NEEDED WARMTH RATHER THAN A REWRITE. The six steps were already plain and good; what was missing was a welcome, and the explanation of compiler, shell and proof AS A READER MEETS THEM rather than assumed. Plus one sentence of why it matters -- a computer you can read all the way down can hold what matters to you without asking you to trust anyone.
loom bhakta_reach before_lap=4 after_door=8 pages_written_in_it=3
loom qa readme register=86 composite=93 first_hour register=87 composite=95 setting=door
loom readme metrics_block_intact=yes links_ok=yes reach_broken=0
file README.md the front door in Bhakta, with the reference half left in Gauge and the badge changed
file docs-geode/tutorials/the-first-hour.md the welcome, the words explained on meeting, and the why
scope one Aether lap -- a register given a door, then the front door itself, then the page it calls join here
status GREEN -- tracked links ok, ascii ok, readme_reach zero broken, metrics block regenerated clean
recommend keep-going -- edu, study and demos are the next Bhakta leaves and each wants a real rewrite rather than a Style line; the register is earned by being written in.
